SUMMARY:The Flying Ace (Richard E. Norman\, 1926) Centennial Screening
DESCRIPTION:This exciting silent film includes a robbery investigation\, 
 love story\, and Black pilots before they were legally allowed to earn li
 censes to fly in the United States! Our programming honors actor and stun
 tman\, Steve "Peg" Reynolds\, who had one leg.  On Wednesday\, October 7t
 h\, we'll host a pre-screening reception at the BFCA at 5:00 p.m.\, where
  The Richard E. Norman Collection (https://nam12.safelinks.protection.out
 look.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.list-manage.com%2FlJhQwE1EbcE%3Fe%3Daae39a
 2b17%26c2id%3Ddfc0ca262765e474fd1a5227622ddfb0&amp\;data=05%7C02%7Cbfca%4
 0iu.edu%7Cc505c54d174a42be817a08deffcb84e5%7C1113be34aed14d00ab4bcdd02510
 be91%7C1%7C0%7C639229446766139713%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGk
 iOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3
 D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp\;sdata=RxF3xHCUDmtRUQ4pMtMtctxx8MaRuNJr7cffDizWrTY%
 3D&amp\;reserved=0) will be on display. Immediately following the 7:00 p.
 m. screening of The Flying Ace at IU Cinema\, Dr. Novotny Lawrence will m
 oderate a discussion with experts in the fields of disability studies\, f
 ilm history\, and music composition. Special thanks to our partners: IU C
 inema\, ReelAbilities\, Smithsonian Folklife Festival\, and the Filomen M
 . D'Agostino Greenberg Music School.
